 `approval_policy: "never"` only removes the prompts. What the agent is allowed to touch is `sandbox_mode`. Setting `never` without a sandbox mode gives an unattended agent full access.
 
+When the Codex process runs remotely, set `mcp_servers.paseo.environment_id` to the
+Codex execution environment that can reach your Paseo daemon. The environment must
+already exist in Codex's configuration. This selects where the MCP connection runs;
+Paseo still supplies the session's address and authentication headers. Omit the
+option to use Codex's default MCP routing. You can set it on one custom Codex provider
+under `agents.providers.<id>.options` without changing other providers.
